{
  "case_id": "2008-07-591",
  "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument\nnext in Case 07-591, Melendez-Diaz v. Massachusetts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: In your answer, you said,\nwell, there would be this stack of affidavits and that's\nall the State would have to do. I think, Mr. Fisher, that was not quite responsive because the question here\nis whether or not there is an exception for business records."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Fisher, how many States\ndo things the way -- the way you would have them done?\nI mean, how many States don't have these -- these notice laws, but in fact bring in the analyst to -- to give the\ninformation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What does that fact support -- why does that fact support your argument, that in all of those cases you're arguing for what's going to be an empty exercise?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Fisher, I am interested in the history since that's what the Court held in Crawford, that the content of the Confrontation Clause is not what we would like it to be, but what it historically was when it was enshrined in the Constitution. As a matter of history, was there a business records exception, not from the hearsay rule but from the Confrontation Clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General Coakley. ORAL ARGUMENT OF MARTHA COAKLEY ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, do you have to have a machine? I mean, what about -- what about ballistics? \"This bullet came from that gun.\" Does that involve sufficient discretion, sufficient judgment that the expert has to be there, while the blood -- blood or drug testing doesn't?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Coakley",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I address that, Your Honor, by saying that for Massachusetts it would be an undue burden with very little benefit to the defendant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So just because the machine is involved it seems to me we cannot make a sensible rule based on that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Yes but the rule, the issue is not limited to drug cases. Murder cases, all sorts of cases where there is scientific evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. Schertler (Government)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SCHERTLER: Yes, Mr. Chief Justice for the following reason. Just as in the case of the records custodians, a defendant may believe that that is not an authentic record; and nothing about the rule we propose would prevent the defense from challenging the authenticity or the circumstances, the correctness of the testing procedures that were used."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Could you comment on the California experience, please?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: So you say they could introduce the squiggly line and put on the stand an analyst who says what that squiggly line shows is that this was cocaine?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey L. Fisher (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Let me start, Your Honors: If there is any doubt remaining about the machine-generated theory that the Solicitor General was putting forward today, again I would refer the court back to the scientific evidence treatise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: No, no, there's a hearsay -- there is a hearsay aspect. I'm not saying it's the only thing. There is a chain and so forth but, there is a hearsay aspect to that which you see, okay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "50ad870ec72f2d84abc1ecd5d19e8c1e8f31b58f71e35ecaf253be96530425be",
      "evidence_id": "ev-50ad870ec72f-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Why don't you insist, even in that case, on the confrontation right to examine the person who actually conducted the test itself and generated the papers that the later expert testifies on in order to determine the admissibility of the -- of the -- the test results themselves?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-591",
      "confidence": 0.0,
